description:
I have only the minor (no patch) R version set up in a project. `rig rstudio` seems to stumble when reading the version from `renv.lock`:

```sh
$ rig rstudio project.Rproj
[ERROR] Invalid R version in renv.lock file: "4.3", unexpected end of input while parsing minor version number
```

Here is what the corresponding part of `renv.lock` looks like:

```json
{
  "R": {
    "Version": "4.3",
    "Repositories": [
      {
        "Name": "CRAN",
        "URL": "https://packagemanager.posit.co/cran/latest"
      }
    ]
  },
```

@ankane wtr https://github.com/r-lib/rig/issues/307 do you think it would be possible to include the rig menu bar app in the brew package? Or should that go into a different package?

Btw. it is not so great that the formula is called rig-r and the Linux package is called r-rig. Do you know if there is a process for renaming a homebrew package, assuming the r-rig name is ok?

cc @jeroen https://github.com/r-lib/rig/pull/318
